    <!-- Sources -->
    <string name="feature_profile_sources_intro">The calculated goal follows published adequate intakes for water. The per-kilogram factors and the activity, climate and altitude amounts are this app’s own guidance values, not clinical values.</string>
    <string name="feature_profile_source_efsa">EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies (2010). Scientific Opinion on Dietary Reference Values for water. EFSA Journal 8(3):1459. Used for the adequate intakes by age and gender, and for pregnancy and breastfeeding.</string>
    <string name="feature_profile_source_nasem">US National Academies (2004). Dietary Reference Intakes for Water, Potassium, Sodium, Chloride, and Sulfate. Basis for counting about 80% of total water as drinks.</string>
    <string name="feature_profile_source_acsm">American College of Sports Medicine (2007). Exercise and Fluid Replacement, position stand. Basis for the per-minute exercise allowance.</string>
    <string name="feature_profile_limits">Calculated goals are kept between %1$s and %2$s for adults and %3$s and %4$s for children under 14.</string>
